<title>USA: IES trims 538 MW Iowa nuclear plant output.</title>
<headline>IES trims 538 MW Iowa nuclear plant output.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>IES Utilities reduced output at its 538 megawatt (MW) Duane Arnold nuclear power plant after a recirculation pump tripped, Nuclear Regulatory Commission said Tuesday.</p>
<p>In its daily status report, NRC said the nuclear station, in Palo, Iowa, was currently operating at 82 percent of capacity after production fell to low of 37 percent.</p>
<p>The pump trip stemmed from a breaker malfunction, the NRC said.</p>
<p>IES Utilities is a subsidiary of IES Industries Inc.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk 212-859-1622</p>
</text>
